    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I need to clarify the responsibilities for a contract we are reviewing. We're looking at a shipment of electronic components from South Korea to Germany under CIF Incoterms 2020. Can you explain exactly what the seller is responsible for under CIF?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under Incoterms 2020's CIF (Cost Insurance and Freight) term, the seller (the Korean seller in your case) is responsible for the cost, insurance, and freight of the goods to the named port of destination in Germany. Once the goods are loaded onto the ship, the risk of loss or damage shifts from the seller to the buyer. However, until then, the Korean seller must deliver the goods on board or on the quays. The buyer then takes over upon delivery, assuming responsibility for all costs and risks from that point onwards.",
