    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. One thing that's confusing me is the insurance part. Since the seller pays for it, are they required to provide a specific level of coverage, or can they just pick the cheapest option available to them? I want to make sure our interests are protected once the goods are actually in transit.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller is required to provide insurance coverage for the buyer, ensuring the goods are covered in transit, but it's not specified how much coverage the seller must obtain. Generally, the seller will need to obtain insurance of a standard sufficient to cover the goods against the usual risks of sea transport. It’s important for you to confirm that the level of insurance meets your requirements. Accompanying your contract, you may want to clearly stipulate that the seller should arrange for insurance coverage at least equal to the value of the goods or better. This will ensure your interests are adequately protected.",
